## Exact execution order

### A. Bean Validation on `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (before the method body runs)

DTO `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/.../dto/OwnerFieldsDto.java`. Constraints (annotations on the getters):
- `firstName` (line 142): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `lastName` (line 163): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `address` (line 184): `@Size(min = 1, max = 255)`
- `addressLine1` (line 205): `@Size(max = 255)`
- `addressLine2` (line 226): `@Size(max = 255)`
- `city` (line 247): `@NotNull @Size(min = 1, max = 80)`
- `telephone` (line 268): `@NotNull @Size(min = 1, max = 20)`
- `email` (line 289): `@Size(max = 255) @jakarta.validation.constraints.Email`
- `postcode` (line 310): `@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{4}$")`
- `registrationDate` (line 331): `@Valid`; `birthDate` (line 352): `@Valid`
- `title` is a `TitleEnum` (MR/MRS/MS/DR, lines 34-68); `sharesHousehold` is a write-only `Boolean` with no constraints.

### B. The three custom Spring `Validator`s registered via `@InitBinder` (run in the same `@Valid` pass, errors collected into the same `BindingResult`)

1. `OwnerFieldsValidator` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/OwnerFieldsValidator.java`. Rejects blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and rejects missing address (needs either a structured `addressLine1` or a flat `address`, checked via `AddressResolver.hasStructuredAddress`/`hasFlatAddress`; rejection reported on `addressLine1`). Lines 47-72.
2. `PostcodeValidator` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../PostcodeValidator.java`. Only when postcode is present and 4 digits: rejects (`postcode.outOfRange`) if `RegionPostcodes.isValidForCity(city, postcode)` is false (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099; unknown cities accept any). Lines 42-52.
3. `DisposableEmailDomainValidator` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../DisposableEmailDomainValidator.java`. Rejects (`email.disposableDomain`) if the email's domain is in the disposable list (`DisposableEmailDomains`). Lines 47-54.

Any errors here become `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → handled at 400 (see exception advice).

### C. Method-body steps (in order)

1. `replayIdempotentCreate(idempotencyKey)` → `OwnerIdempotencyStore.find` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../OwnerIdempotencyStore.java`. In-memory `ConcurrentHashMap<String,Integer>`. If key already used, returns original owner with 200 and the create stops here. Lines 39-44.
2. `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` lines 170-178. MapStruct maps DTO → `Owner`, ignoring `id, pets, memberId, householdId, namesakeCount, possibleDuplicate, possibleDuplicateOf, deleted`.
3. `addressResolver.resolve(owner)` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../AddressResolver.java` lines 62-74. Normalizes address fields in place via `AddressNormalizer` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/.../AddressNormalizer.java`: trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST→STREET, RD→ROAD, AVE→AVENUE). Prefers structured `addressLine1`(+`addressLine2`), else flat `address`.
4. `registrationDateValidator.validate(owner.getRegistrationDate())` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../RegistrationDateValidator.java` lines 37-42. Throws `FutureRegistrationDateException` (→ 400) if the supplied date is after `LocalDate.now()`. Null is allowed.
5. Default the registration date to `LocalDate.now()` if null (controller lines 202-203).
6. `businessDayAdjuster.toBusinessDay(registrationDate)` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../BusinessDayAdjuster.java` lines 45-56. Rolls weekends/fixed 2026 public holidays forward to the next business day; result stored on the owner.
7. `telephoneNormalizer.normalize(owner.getTelephone())` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../TelephoneNormalizer.java` lines 59-73. Strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps `+`CC or assumes `+61` (drops one leading `0`); requires 8-15 digits after `+`, then `E164CountryRules.validateNationalLength` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/.../E164CountryRules.java`: +61 → 9 national digits, +1 → 10). Throws `InvalidTelephoneException` (→ 400) on failure. (Also note the `Owner` entity has `@Pattern(regexp="^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$")` on `telephone`, line 58.)
8. `emailNormalizer.normalize(owner.getEmail())` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../EmailNormalizer.java` lines 41-46. Blank → null; else trim + lower-case.
9. `dailyRegistrationLimitValidator.validate(owner.getRegistrationDate())` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../DailyRegistrationLimitValidator.java` lines 48-52. Throws `DailyRegistrationLimitExceededException` (→ 429) if `clinicService.countOwnersRegisteredOn(date) >= 100`.
10. `cityCapacityValidator.validate(owner)` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../CityCapacityValidator.java` lines 46-50. Throws `CityCapacityExceededException` (→ 409) if `clinicService.countOwnersInCity(city) >= 50` (case-insensitive count).
11. `owner.setHouseholdId(households.householdId(owner))` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../Households.java` lines 70-74. `householdId` = first 12 hex of `SHA-256(V2 + '|' + normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`.
12. `duplicateIdentityValidator.validate(owner)` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../DuplicateIdentityValidator.java` lines 49-57. Computes `OwnerIdentity.key` and throws `DuplicateIdentityException` (→ 409) if any non-deleted existing owner shares the same identity key. `OwnerIdentity` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/.../OwnerIdentity.java` lines 52-58) = `SHA-256(V2 + '|' + telephone + '|' + email + '|' + soundex(lastName))`.
13. Soft-duplicate branch (controller lines 211-217): if `sharesHousehold == true`, set `possibleDuplicate = false`; otherwise `possibleDuplicateDetector.detect(owner)` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../PossibleDuplicateDetector.java` lines 56-77. Sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest non-deleted owner with a different identity key but same postcode and same last-name Soundex. Never blocks creation.

### D. Persistence + service-layer side effects

`this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` `saveOwner`, lines 248-266, `@Transactional`:
```java
if (owner.isNew() && owner.getMemberId() == null) {
    String region = Locality.forOwner(owner) + OwnerIdentityVersion.TAG;
    int fiscalYear = FiscalYear.containing(owner.getRegistrationDate()).shortYear();
    String baseId = memberIdGenerator.generate(region, fiscalYear, owner.getTelephone(), owner.getLastName());
    List<String> existingIds = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
        .map(Owner::getMemberId).filter(Objects::nonNull).toList();
    owner.setMemberId(memberIdDeduplicator.deDuplicate(baseId, existingIds));
}
if (owner.isNew() && owner.getNamesakeCount() == null) {
    Collection<Owner> sameLastName = ownerRepository.findByLastNameIgnoreCase(owner.getLastName());
    owner.setNamesakeCount(namesakeCounter.count(owner, sameLastName));
}
ownerRepository.save(owner);
```
Side effects generated at save time:
- `memberId` via `MemberIdGenerator` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/MemberIdGenerator.java`): `<REGION><FY><HASH8><LuhnCheck>`, then de-duplicated by `MemberIdDeduplicator` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/.../MemberIdDeduplicator.java`, appends `-n`).
- `namesakeCount` via `NamesakeCounter` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/.../NamesakeCounter.java`): count of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).

Repository methods called during creation: `ownerRepository.findAll()` (for memberId dedup), `ownerRepository.findByLastNameIgnoreCase(...)` (namesakes), and `ownerRepository.save(owner)`. Interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`; Spring Data impl with queries: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` (profile `spring-data-jpa`). JPA (`JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`) and JDBC (`JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`) alternatives also exist under other profiles.
Also indirectly, the earlier validators call `clinicService.countOwnersRegisteredOn`, `countOwnersInCity`, `findOwnerByLastNameIgnoreCase`, and `findAllOwners`, each of which iterates `ownerRepository.findAll()` (see `ClinicServiceImpl` lines 138-343).

### E. Post-save side effects (still inside the request)

1. `ownerAuditLogger.logCreated(owner)` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../OwnerAuditLogger.java` lines 61-67. Emits two lines to the `AUDIT` logger: a human-readable line (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel) and a JSON-serialized `OwnerCreatedEvent` with a monotonic sequence number. No DB write, no event bus.
2. `welcomeNotifier.enqueueWelcome(owner)` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../WelcomeNotifier.java` lines 39-42. Logs one line to the `NOTIFY` logger (ownerId, memberId). Just a log line.
3. `ownerIdempotencyStore.record(idempotencyKey, owner.getId())` — records the key→id mapping (first write wins). Lines 50-55 of `OwnerIdempotencyStore.java`.
4. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` — builds the response DTO. This mapper (`OwnerMapper` lines 47-65) computes many derived read-only fields (selfLink, apiVersion, identity, displayName, salutation, initials, telephoneDisplay, fiscalYear, membershipPoints/Level, locality, timezone, bulkSignupWarning, capacityWarning, riskFlag, contactPreference, ageBand, ownerSegment) — these are output-shaping, not persistence.
5. `Location` header set to `/api/owners/{id}`, response `201 CREATED`.

