## Domain / entity classes

- `Owner` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`. `@Entity @Table(name="owners")`, extends `Person`. Validation annotations: `address` `@NotEmpty` (43-44), `city` `@NotEmpty` (53-54), `telephone` `@NotEmpty @Pattern(...E.164...)` (56-59), `email` `@Email` (61-63). Persisted fields include `title, addressLine1/2, postcode, memberId, registrationDate, birthDate, householdId, namesakeCount, possibleDuplicate, possibleDuplicateOf, deleted`, plus `@OneToMany pets`. No `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`.
- `Person` (`@MappedSuperclass`) — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../model/Person.java`: `firstName` `@NotEmpty` (31-33), `lastName` `@NotEmpty` (35-37).
- `BaseEntity` (`@MappedSuperclass`) — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../model/BaseEntity.java`: `@Id @GeneratedValue(IDENTITY) Integer id`; `isNew()` returns `id == null`.

## Validation-groups / `@Validated`

- No Bean Validation groups are used anywhere for owner creation (no `groups=` attributes).
- `@Validated` appears at class level on the generated `OwnersApi` interface (enables method-parameter validation). The custom validators are plain Spring `org.springframework.validation.Validator` implementations wired through `@InitBinder`, not JSR-380 `ConstraintValidator`s. (The only custom `ConstraintValidator` in the project, `PetAgeValidator` under `rest/validation/`, applies to pets, not owners.)

